      <div class="content-grid">
        <div class="content-card">
          <h3>Hard Court Surfaces</h3>
          <p>The most popular choice for residential and club facilities. Hard courts offer consistent ball bounce, require less maintenance than other surfaces, and can be customized with color combinations and cushioning systems.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Acrylic surface systems</li>
            <li>Cushioned layer options</li>
            <li>Multiple color combinations</li>
            <li>All-weather durability</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="content-card">
          <h3>Clay Court Alternatives</h3>
          <p>While traditional clay courts require intensive maintenance, modern clay-like surfaces provide similar playing characteristics with reduced upkeep. These surfaces offer slower ball speeds and higher bounces.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Har-Tru green clay systems</li>
            <li>Synthetic clay alternatives</li>
            <li>Natural red clay options</li>
            <li>Specialized drainage systems</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="content-card">
          <h3>Grass Court Alternatives</h3>
          <p>Synthetic turf systems designed for tennis provide the fast, low-bounce characteristics of grass courts without the extensive maintenance requirements of natural grass surfaces.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Professional-grade synthetic turf</li>
            <li>Specialized infill systems</li>
            <li>Consistent ball behavior</li>
            <li>Minimal maintenance needs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
